WEBVTT

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.860
Hey Riri, where do you want to go when you're in college?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.490
How about you?

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:21.290
Tibet, I think, and then Indonesia, Thailand, Vietnam, Turkey,

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:27.130
Egypt, Tunisia, Spain, Portugal, and, um... Morocco!

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.130
But I can't really afford it.

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:34.090
Don't get so caught up in backpacking that you drop out.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.930
You're going to Europe, right?

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.930
I'm going to Florence.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.050
I want to experience the Italian Renaissance through their museums,

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:44.310
see the cathedral's architecture, and attend an opera at La Scala.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.310
But I can't really afford it.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.900
Such a lady of leisure, Riri!

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.980
Why "lady"?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.530
Because of your ladylike calm.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.280
One boy and one girl.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.260
What about a husband?

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.700
What, you want one?

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.950
Never said I didn't.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.070
Hey, wanna go over some English later?

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.460
Yeah, sure.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.730
Once we graduate, let's go to Okinawa!

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.460
If we graduate.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.470
We can't really afford it anyway.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:17.050
Five

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:18.050
Four

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.010
Three

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:20.010
Two

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:21.020
One

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.470
I've gotta get up and make something for Sae.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:22.950
That smells nice.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.970
Silly Misato.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:47.810
Sesame seeds?

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.060
...seeds?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.330
...seeds?

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.560
...seeds?

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.950
Good morning, Sae.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:55.940
Good morning.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.700
Hey, did you see something scattered on your doorstep this morning?

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.740
Yeah, it has to be something—

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.960
Sae, Hiro, good morning.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.370
Good morning, Riri.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.040
Good morning.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.670
Morning, everyone.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.340
Good morning, Misato.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.050
You did it again, didn't you?

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.220
Yeah.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.100
What's your theme this time?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.600
A visualization of time.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.610
Or maybe something like a conceptualization of motion.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.360
I've just got to look for all the possibilities art opens up!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.530
I thought maybe it was a superstition.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:45.830
Misato, you shouldn't waste food like that.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.120
Make sure you clean it up later.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.040
Sure.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.040
Art Dept.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.040
We're sketching today.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.540
The theme is, um... something in the classroom.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.050
You'll be judged based on your selection of motif.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.550
Of course, you're welcome to use me.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:07.430
Yes, how about "a maiden gazing out the window in winter" for your theme?

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.600
The word melancholy sounds so wonderful.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:17.960
Don't you think this would be perfect as a theme today?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.110
Hurry up and get back to teaching.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.860
Miss Yoshinoya.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:35.040
Can you please take the lessons more seriously?

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:39.300
But the sky today is so blue.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.460
Sae?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.390
What's wrong, Sae?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.980
Oh, sorry.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.740
You've been dozing a lot in class lately.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.950
Is something keeping you up at night?

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.410
No, it's not really...

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:11.410
You're still only sixteen. You're growing, so you shouldn't strain yourself.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.660
Sorry. I'll be more careful.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:16.540
A lack of sleep is the enemy of beauty!

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.550
I also have to be careful not to talk on the phone too long!

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.470
Sae, did you get any sleep last night?

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.310
Yeah, I fell asleep at my desk.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.030
I'm done.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:41.230
I'm glad I got that rookie prize, but then they wanted me to write another one.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.610
But that's great!

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.920
I got all flustered writing it, and they rejected the one after that.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:53.250
I don't know if I can keep this up.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:06:02.000
You know your editor's only that harsh because she knows you can do better.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.310
I'm really looking forward to your next story.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:11.260
I don't think anyone else can match the tender, gentle atmosphere.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:22.280
What's up?

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.650
Oh, Natsume.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:27.440
I think she's just worn out.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.820
Sorry!

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.100
I've gotta keep trying.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.160
Yeah, keep trying.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:05.360
This is good.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.240
Coming!

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:15.080
Hiro, can I borrow some soy sauce?

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:17.960
I lied, I really need white-out.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.460
Smells good in here.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.550
I'm making beef stew.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.940
I wrote something wrong on the application form for the design concours.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.850
Here you go. Is that enough?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.600
Thanks. I'll bring it back later.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.330
Sorry, I forgot.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.330
I'm headed off to cram school.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.010
Let's do the English later.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:06.240
Sure, sure.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.590
Guess there's no choice.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.350
Sae, you alive in there?

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.400
It's so warm.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.780
Sorry you had to make me dinner.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:35.280
I don't mind. It's the same amount of work as if I only cooked for myself.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.540
And it tastes better when you eat together, doesn't it?

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:39.040
Yeah.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.370
So, is it going well?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.870
Yeah, I feel like I've got something.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:49.000
That's great. You always try a little too hard.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.010
Really?

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.280
Remember field day?

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:59.510
You had the mumps, and even though your cheeks were all puffy, you insisted on going.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.020
You probably would've gone if I hadn't stopped you.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.610
Maybe I should move in next to you.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.400
The leases here run a year, right?

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.530
Yeah, I think so.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.830
That way, I could check on you just by tapping on the wall.

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.830
We have cell phones for that now, you know.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.830
Besides, I already rely on you a lot.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.670
Maybe a little too much.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.540
That's why you're able to try as hard as you do.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:35.430
Don't worry about it. We're friends, right?

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.680
Thanks.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.580
Now that you mention it, Misato came by last night.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:47.510
She sure is a strange one, always looking for ways to have fun.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:51.190
It always gets me excited wondering what she'll do next.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.970
Like this morning.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:57.700
Oh yeah, remember when she tried to do Hidamari Apartments up Arabian-style?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.200
Yeah, she drew O's and X's all over the doors in chalk.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.230
The landlady was so mad at her.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:14.970
Hello?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.080
'Sup!

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.470
You got any stew left?

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.970
Why did you come to my room looking for...

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.980
I could smell it.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.290
Good evening, Misato.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.100
There's still plenty of stew left.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.400
Would you like some?

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:36.900
Can I?

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.660
Come right in.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:42.660
Would you like a salad too?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.630
It's great to have younger people around.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.420
You've gotten really good at cooking, Hiro.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.080
Not really.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:53.620
She'd make a great wife, you know.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.090
What's that supposed to mean!?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.720
Nothing wrong with that.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.410
Everyone gets along so well at Hidamari Apartments.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:05.350
I feel so lonely every time I think about how I'm going to be gone next year.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.850
Well, at least if I manage to graduate.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:14.360
That again? Riri's been talking about all the concours you've received awards at.

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:18.100
It's all spray and pray.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:23.620
Plus, there's no keeping me from having fun with all those challenges.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.660
That was great!

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.570
You're welcome.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:33.170
Anyone want coffee?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.680
I can't get this story out of my head.

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.930
I wonder if I'm really able to do this.

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.180
Won't know until you try, right?

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:52.760
Just do what you love.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:54.890
You're still a first year, right?

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:59.070
Never mind thinking. Stick up an antenna and get to work!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.490
An antenna?

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.090
Yeah, the antenna of your design sense.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.990
That's what the art program is all about.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.700
You're so serious, Sae.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.620
You just can't leave her alone when she's like this either, can you, Hiro?

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:17.120
Me? Well, I guess.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.130
Though I don't really get why.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:26.510
Riri always gets angry and says, "It's not like I'm
at Hidamari Apartments just to look after you!"

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.560
Really?

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.850
She's always smiling, and she seems so mature.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:34.650
I really look up to her.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:38.930
That's just Riri's pose. She looks almost like a guy when she does it.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:40.860
Yeah, I see what you mean.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.610
Misato, you there?

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:46.130
Don't go spreading rumors now.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:47.870
Yeah, she's here.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.660
Sorry to bother you, Sae.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.500
I came to get Misato.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.000
Misato, time to work on your English!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.010
Sorry, I'm coming.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.870
That was great.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:05.390
I'll make curry next time, so you two should come over and have some.

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:07.640
I'll make it nice and spicy for you.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.890
Sure.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:10.520
See you tomorrow.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.020
Good night.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.520
Good night.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.020
Good night.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.490
We talked so much.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:29.740
I wonder if Sae's still up writing.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.160
She was so tired today. Maybe she'll rest tonight.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:44.170
I can't stop thinking of her, can I?

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:48.680
I need to worry about myself too.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:51.430
But I won't know until I try.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:55.710
Misato said to get to work.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:14:01.070
Maybe I'll get up early tomorrow and bring her some french toast.

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:03.940
With strawberry jam, maybe.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.950
November 22nd
"Third Years and
First Years"

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.950
To be
continued

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.950
The end

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.460
Happy morning!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.080
One, two, three, four!

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.970
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.070
Ichi, ni, san, shi!

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.970
Go, roku, shichi, hachi!

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.980
Yi, er, san, si!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.980
Wu, liu, qi, ba!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.890
Chinese?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:42.980
May 21st

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:42.980
"The Weeping
Woman"

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:48.240
The weather feels great!

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:58.460
Sorry, I got carried away and made too many sandwiches.

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:05.460
I wanted to have a picnic with you anyway, so I'm glad it's sunny.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:10.470
I guess I should've worn pants if I wanted to do that, though.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.460
Miss Yoshinoya, you're supposed to be teaching.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.220
Right.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.130
Okay, today we're working on landscapes.

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:21.190
I'd like you to use objects in the park as your motif,

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:24.230
and light and shadow as your theme.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:28.740
We'll go back to school in the afternoon
for finishing work and a presentation,

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:33.530
so be sure to make plenty of sketches and work out some ideas this morning.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:37.040
Meet back here at 11:30, okay?

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:43.790
And even though you're free until then, take the lesson seriously.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.300
She's talking to herself?

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:52.550
Light and shadow... [hikari to kage]
What should I use for a motif?

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.760
There's plenty of options.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.520
Light... lizard.
[hikari tokage]

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.270
Yunocchi, you're such a punster.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:06.270
I wasn't thinking that!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.990
Look, Yunocchi! A playground!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.240
Wow, you're right!

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.190
I'll start with this!

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:18.240
Come on, Miya, we have to draw.

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.840
That was pretty tough.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.260
Come on, Miya...

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.010
A subject, a subject...

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:36.010
The slide's shadow looks pretty interesting.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.980
Look over here, Miya! There's koi!

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.150
Fish?

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.650
Look at their mouths flap!

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:52.900
I wonder why they're doing that.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:57.910
They probably think they can get food since there's people here.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.410
Miya!?

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:06.420
It's pretty tough to hit.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.180
What are you doing?

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:09.610
Oh, Yuno!

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:11.420
We're aiming for the Weeping Woman.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.670
Woman?

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:16.670
You shouldn't be mean like that.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:19.790
I can't see her, but... but...

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:24.290
No, Yuno, look at that.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.480
That rock sticking up out of the water.

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:32.930
They say that if you hit it with a rock, you'll get better at drawing.

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.620
It's because it looks like Picasso's <i>Weeping Woman.</i>

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.830
So, it's throwing the rocks out with the bathwater.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.660
Yeah, I guess.

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.330
Sure.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:48.080
I shouldn't have said that.

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:51.090
Yunocchi, let's give it a try!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.840
Fine, but only once.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.180
Aw, so close.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.970
Wow!

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.770
Okay, let's go, Yunocchi.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.150
You want to try again?

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.570
Yes! I hit it!

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.080
I can't do it.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.580
Maybe with a bigger stone...

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.340
What are you all doing?

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.180
Oh, Miss Yoshinoya.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.430
They say that if you hit that rock with a stone, you'll get better at drawing!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.930
I see.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.170
All right, I'll try too!

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.440
But that one's a bit small.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:55.070
That's just uncanny.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:04.120
Okay everyone, we'll be commenting on your presentation at 4:00, so get to work.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.500
Huh?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.460
'Sup?

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:08.370
My hand...

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:13.130
Could this be the curse of the Weeping Woman!?

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.630
Isn't that ironic?

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.630
All right, time's up.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.640
Pass your work to the front.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:29.640
Don't cry.

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:31.900
That's definitely light and shadow.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.400
Mine too.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:41.970
I did something silly.

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:43.420
That's unfortunate.

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:45.360
Want to borrow my hot water bottle?

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.500
Nah, I don't need it.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.750
The classes must be fun in the art program.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:53.510
Gen Ed sounds fun too.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:57.590
You have lots of clubs we don't, like band.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.840
Um, Yuno, can I see your hand for a second?

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:05.470
This is the pressure point on your hand.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:08.810
Did it hurt?

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.230
No, it was just a shock.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:15.730
The kanji for the pressure point in the hand is a combination of "pass" and "palm."

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.740
This is good for when your hands get tired.

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:20.710
How's that?

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:23.050
It feels a lot looser now.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:24.940
Thanks, Nazuna.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.740
You're welcome. Mom taught me how to do it.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.890
Nazuna, do me too!

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:31.000
Me too!

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:33.960
You're going to have to take turns.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.960
I'll be able to draw like normal again tomorrow.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.950
May 21st

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.950
The end

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.950
To be continued

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:46.930
Yunocchi, I'm
leaving a towel
and some clothes
out for you.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:46.930
Thanks!

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:43.620
Let's be brave and face reality!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.470
What do I do?

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.550
What's wrong? You look sick.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.740
Is something bothering you?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.480
...Huh?

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:49.170
We won't know if you don't tell us.

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:50.390
Well, um...

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:52.810
If there's anything I can do to help...

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.360
That's right! Don't just keep it bottled up!

00:20:54.930 --> 00:21:01.980
Miya, how do you
have a change of
panties for me?

00:20:54.930 --> 00:21:01.980
Oh!

00:20:55.360 --> 00:21:00.820
Um, I swallowed a plum pit. Am I going to be okay?

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.690
Next time, "May 28th~June 2nd: Sunshine Palette."

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:09.810
I grabbed
your
laundry
off your
balcony.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:09.810
Eh!?!

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:09.810
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
